Reason:
When `i` equals `optlen - 1` (the last byte of the options area) and `op[i] >= 2`, the expression `op[i+1]` reads one byte past the end of the buffer, causing an out‑of‑bounds access. The missing check for `i == optlen - 1` allows this condition to occur.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
